# Keep line endings stable across operating systems.
#
# The Gradle wrapper and shell scripts are executed by /bin/sh — including inside the Linux build
# containers — so they MUST be LF on every OS. Without this, a Windows checkout (autocrlf) gets them
# in CRLF and the shebang breaks ("./gradlew: not found" during `docker build`). `eol=lf` forces LF
# everywhere: Mac/Linux are unaffected (already LF), Windows checkouts stop getting CRLF. The committed
# blobs are already LF, so no re-normalization of existing files is needed.
*.sh        text eol=lf
gradlew     text eol=lf

# Windows batch scripts must stay CRLF.
*.bat       text eol=crlf
gradlew.bat text eol=crlf
